== A7 theorem (Lambda-units): algebraic x  ==>  a0^2/(G rho_L) = (8 pi/3) K^2 transcendental ==
  ok   a0^2/(G rho_L) = 1/4  <=>  K^2 = 3/(32 pi) 
  ok   K = sqrt(3/(32 pi)) is NOT algebraic (sympy assumptions: pi transcendental) 
  ok   kappa_b L = K  <=>  x = (sqrt(K^2 + 3) - K)/3 (algebraic iff K is); K = 1/Z gives x_b = (sqrt(1+32 pi) - 1)/sqrt(96 pi) 
  ok   consistency: kappa_b(x) at that x equals K (round trip) 

